-- Clothing furni that may be converted into a Relic, taken from the shipped assets.
--
-- Regenerate with tools/catalog_converter/scan_mintable_nft_clothing.py. Do not
-- hand-edit: an operator's changes belong in the dashboard, which writes this same
-- table, and this file is INSERT IGNORE so it never overwrites them.
--
-- Selected by the classname prefix 'clothing_nft', which is Habbo's own marking for
-- artwork tied to their NFT collections and the only signal in the shipped data that
-- separates them from the other clothing furni.
--
-- The prices and the window are round placeholders and not recovered values: Habbo's
-- own stamp price for a given item is in none of the shipped assets. One stamp, an
-- open edition, and a window that closes in 2099 -- which is how 'no deadline' has to
-- be written, because ends_at is required and the client disables the collect button
-- the moment it passes.
--
-- Minting also costs stamps the player has to own: see nft_mint_token_offers.sql,
-- without which this list is priced in a currency nobody can obtain.
--
-- 429 classnames.

